## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop:** Single `state` object; `rand(state)` wraps `mulberry32Step` and is the only randomness source (searched — no `Math.random` in game logic); `resolveTurn()` calls systems in fixed documented order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map:** `generateGrid()` builds 8x8 via `rand(state)` weighted terrain; `canBuild()` checks `def.terrain.indexOf(tile.terrain)`; `adjacencyBonus()` feeds `adj.mult` into `resolveProduction()` output formula. Score 2.

**F3 — Economy:** ash→soil→food inside `greenhouse` block, ore→metal in forge block, metal→parts in workshop block; `storageCap()`+`addResource()` clamp and log overflow. Score 2.

**F4 — Population:** colonists have `skill`, `fatigue`, `morale`, `job`, `assignedTile`; `workerFactor()` reads `skillMult(c.skill)`/`fatigueMult(c.fatigue)`, used in every production block. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs:** `resolveNeedsAndFatigue()` subtracts food/water, applies `moraleDelta` on shortage, `moraleMult()` read in `workerFactor()`; morale recovers +3 when needs met. Score 2.

**F6 — Research:** `RESEARCH` has 10 nodes; `researchStatus()`/`canStartResearch()` enforce `prereq`; `applyResearchEffect()` writes `researchEffects` read via `researchMult()` in production and `def.requiresResearch` gate. Score 2.

**F7 — Events:** `EVENT_KEYS` has 14 entries; `maybeFireEvent()` does weighted selection (`totalWeight`/`acc`); 5 events (`wanderers`, `old_cache`, `water_contamination`, `colonist_dispute`, `research_opportunity`) have 2-3 differing choice branches; `state.events.cooldowns[chosen]` gates re-fire. Score 2.

**F8 — Trade:** `tradePrice()` reads `stockRatio` (player stock/cap) and `state.trade.drift[res]` (drifts each turn in `tickTrade`); `doTradeBuy`/`doTradeSell` both mutate state and caravan `item.qty` is capped. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard:** `maybeStorm()` fires on `state.nextStorm`, severity scales with `state.turn*0.4`; `dmgMult=t.building.hp/100` reduces every production block's output; `storm_shelters` research sets `stormDamageMult`; `doRepair()` spends `parts`. Score 2.

**F10 — Save/load:** `exportBtn` → `JSON.stringify(GAME,null,2)` into textarea; `importBtn` → `JSON.parse` + `validateState()` writes readable error to `#saveError`. Score 2.

**F11 — End conditions:** `checkEndConditions()` has reachable win (`turn>=60 && colonists>=12 && food/water>=0`) and lose (`colonists.length===0`, driven by morale-based departures); `computeScore()` combines pop/research/turn/stock; `renderEndScreen()` shows summary. Score 2.

**F12 — UI:** `renderTabs()`+click handlers switch tabs; log lines show `T'+e.turn`; `title` attributes power a real tooltip system (`tooltipForResource`, `tileTooltip`); `keydown` handles Space and 1-5; `@media (max-width:480px)` adapts layout. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel:** `runTests()` asserts real invariants (research prereq lock, storage overflow clamp+log, save/load hash round-trip, win/lose reachability); `runHeadlessBenchmark()` runs 200 turns with `greedyPolicyTick` and prints `stateHash()` twice for determinism check. Score 2.

**G1:** `applyResearchEffect` writes e.g. `researchEffects.condenserMult`; `researchMult(state,def.researchMultKey)` multiplies directly into `out=` formula in `resolveProduction`. Fully wired, real formula, every turn. Score 4.

**G2:** shortage (`foodShort`/`waterShort`) → `moraleDelta -=12` in `resolveNeedsAndFatigue` → `c.morale` → `moraleMult(c.morale)` read in `workerFactor()` used by all production blocks next turn. Score 4.

**G3:** `maybeStorm()` sets `t.building.hp` down → `dmgMult=t.building.hp/100` cuts output in every production block → `doRepair()` spends `parts`, restores `hp=100`. Full chain, minor one-idle-colonist gate. Score 4.

**G4:** `tradePrice()` reads `stockRatio=(resources[res]/cap)` and `state.trade.drift[res]` (updated stochastically each `tickTrade`, also nudged by `merchant_rumor` event). Score 4.

**G5:** `wanderers` option "Welcome them in" pushes real `makeColonist` records + spends food/water; `old_cache` options give differing scrip/parts amounts and cost differently — all durable `state.resources`/`state.colonists` writes, not just log text. Score 4.

